280d8824 [deepseek-flash] #The realistic bug: worker passes `if(fd==-1)` (fd=7), then main closes fd 7 and sets fd=-1, then a new accept gets fd 7. Worker then calls `recv(fd,...)` — it reads `fd` again (it's a member, read at call time) which is now -1 → EBADF. OK so actually it'd get EBADF. Unless the compiler hoisted the load. So mostly benign-ish, but UB and the double-close race is the real one.
