280d8827 [deepseek-flash] #For a double-close of the same fd, both threads must call `closeHandle` and both must observe `fd > -1`. `closeHandle` sets `fd=-1` after closing. Since main holds the lock while calling closeHandle, and the worker only calls closeHandle after releasing the lock (post-remove), the two closeHandle calls are ordered by the mutex *if* the worker's remove and main's iteration overlap. If main iterates and finds the connection, it closes it; the worker must then wait for the lock to remove, so the worker's closeHandle comes strictly after main's. So the worker sees fd==-1. No double close.
280d8827 [deepseek-flash] #
280d8827 [deepseek-flash] #But: the worker's `closeHandle` is not under the lock. Suppose the worker removes itself (lock acquired, removed, released) and then is preempted *before* calling closeHandle. Main starts `closeHttpTasks`, acquires the lock, iterates — the connection is no longer in the list, so main doesn't call closeHandle on it. Worker then calls closeHandle. Fine.
280d8827 [deepseek-flash] #
